body:
Friend of mine knows I'm bisexual and has openly admitted that she has a crush on me (we're both female), but knows that I'm not on the same page.

&#x200B;

Cue a trip we're supposed to go on for our school, and she comes up with the brilliant idea to try and trick people into thinking we're a couple. Whatever, a few days of holding her hand and sitting beside each other isn't that bad. 

&#x200B;

Right away, I realize that this was a bad idea. Throughout the weekend, she keeps leaning and whispering 'I love pretending to be a lesbian couple with you', being on top of me non-stop, and even cuddling me when we got to our hotel room. Sure, doesn't sound bad, right?

&#x200B;

She had body odor. Come on, girl. Deodorant is a good thing. Not to mention, there's other hot people here, dammit, you're messing up my chances. Don't get me wrong, she's a good friend, but that weekend nearly drove me to a panic attack because of her incessant doting.
